-- title:
--   Geometric Frobenius sends the place jmath̃=a to jmath̃=a^q
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic a prime $q$, and let `data : ModularPolynomialData q` consist of a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic, of degree $\psi(q)=\sum_{d \mid q,\ d\ \text{squarefree}} q/d$ in its outer variable, and satisfies $\Phi(j(q\cdot),\,j)=0$ as an identity of Laurent series, obtained by evaluating the coefficient polynomials at the $q$-expansion of $j$. Assume `hKr`, the Kronecker congruence: the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ coefficientwise equals $(C(X)^{q}-X)\,(C(X)-X^{q})$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/q)[X][Y]$. Fix $a \in k$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $k$ generated by the two reductions `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`, and recall that a place of $F$ over $k$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $k$, distinct from $F$, and a principal ideal ring. Let `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` be the place of $F$ obtained by transporting, along the $k$-algebra isomorphism `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC` between $k(T)$ and $F$, the finite place of $k(T)$ attached to the irreducible polynomial $T - a$. Let `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel k 1 data hKr` be the map on places of $F$ given by restricting a place to the image of $F$ under the $q$-power $q$-expansion map and transporting the result back along the isomorphism of $F$ with that image. The assertion is that this map sends `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` to `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k (a ^ q)`.
--
--   This identifies the action of the geometric Frobenius on the rational points of the $j$-line in characteristic $q$: the place $\tilde\jmath = a$ is carried to $\tilde\jmath = a^{q}$, with no perfectness assumption on $k$. It is the companion of the statement that the same map fixes the place at infinity, and is used in the specialisation and place-prolongation arguments for modular curves at level one.
